[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Traxler Counterattack"]
[Variation "Traxler: 5.Nxf7 Bxf2+ 6.Kxf2 Nxe4+ 7.Kg1"]
[ECO "C57"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "black"]
[Tricks "trap,mate-threat"]
[Themes "king-hunt,piece-activity"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 4... Bc5 5. Nxf7 5... Bxf2+ 6. Kxf2 6... Nxe4+
7. Kg1 7... Qh4 { The queen comes in again, eyeing f2 and g3. Retreating the king does not stop the attack. [%cal Gh4f2] }
8. g3 (8. Qf3 8... Rf8 { When Black cannot find a new threat, ...Rf8 saves the rook from the knight on f7 and attacks that knight. The engine rates this a little better for Black. [%cal Gh8f8,Gf8f7] } 9. Qe3 9... Nf2 10. d4 10... Ng4 11. Qg3 11... Qxg3 12. hxg3) (8. Qf1 8... Rf8 9. d3 9... Nd6) (8. h3 8... Rf8 9. d4 9... Nf2 10. Bg5 10... Qxg5) (8. Qe2 8... Nd4 9. Qe3 9... Nc2 10. Qe2 10... Nd4) (8. Nd6+ 8... Nxd6) (8. Nxh8? 8... Qf2#) 8... Nxg3 { Takes the pawn and opens lines against the king. }
9. hxg3 (9. Nxh8 9... Nd4 10. Bf7+ 10... Ke7 11. hxg3 11... Qxg3+ 12. Kf1 12... d6) (9. Ng5 9... Qxg5 10. Bf7+ 10... Kxf7) 9... Qxg3+ { Check. The queen takes a pawn and keeps the king boxed in. } 10. Kf1 10... Rf8 { Attacks the knight on f7, which is pinned against the king on f1. The engine calls this about equal, so it is a hard defence for White. [%cal Gf8f7] }
11. Nc3 (11. d4 11... d5 12. Bxd5 12... Bh3+ 13. Rxh3 13... Qxh3+ 14. Kg1 14... Qg3+) (11. Bd5 11... Nb4 12. Qe1 12... Qf4) 11... d5 { Opens the bishop on c8 and hits the bishop on c4. } 12. Bxd5 12... Bh3+ { Brings the last piece in with check. White must find several accurate moves. [%cal Gc8h3] } *
